## Transitive dependencies

`package-lock.json` pins the full install tree. Each of those packages carries
its own licence and copyright notice inside its own tarball; npm installs them,
and they are not shipped here. Counts as resolved by this project's lockfile:

| License | Packages |
|---|---|
| MIT | 85 |
| ISC | 7 |
| BSD-3-Clause | 2 (`fast-uri`, `qs`) |
| BSD-2-Clause | 1 (`json-schema-typed`) |

If you redistribute an installed `node_modules` tree, reproduce the licence text
that each package ships in its own directory.

## Inspiration

The tool shape and the approach of wrapping a coding CLI in an MCP server were
inspired by
[`deepseek-claude-code-worker-mcp`](https://github.com/louchi1984-coder/deepseek-claude-code-worker-mcp)
(MIT), which does the same job for Claude Code. No code was copied from it; it
is credited here as prior art.
